GENIE PNI
ILM-GENIE — Integrative Linguistic Multiscript Meta-Cycler
Version: 1.0.0
Status: Canonical working architectural specification
Scope: Humanesque ILM / linguistic / expressive / multiscript / computational equity
Governing principle: RETRIEVE, DON'T RECONSTRUCT

============================================================
0. CONSTITUTIONAL DEFINITION
============================================================

ILM-GENIE is the GENIE-level meta-cycler for Integrative Linguistic
Multiscript (ILM).

It operates across the full expressive and computational stack while
preserving the two constitutional pillars of ILM:

    I.  REPRESENTATIONAL EQUITY
    II. COMPUTATIONAL EQUITY

ILM-GENIE is not a narrow "language GENIE".

It is an adaptive meta-cycler capable of:

- retrieving authoritative linguistic, cultural, expressive and technical
  material;
- preserving identity, provenance and source distinctions;
- representing and reversibly transforming expressive systems;
- computationalizing those systems without surrendering their identity;
- orchestrating fieldwork and community/source interaction;
- ascending and descending across abstraction levels;
- changing operative disciplinary role as the task requires;
- splitting into specialist GENIEs;
- merging specialist GENIEs into higher-order configurations;
- composing heterogeneous cycles;
- descending into specialist cyclers;
- ascending from local execution into integrative interpretation;
- coordinating science, arts and humanities roles;
- constructing end-to-end deliverables where authorized;
- remaining backend-neutral and infrastructure-agnostic.

Core invariant:

    GENIE ASCENDS TO UNDERSTAND THE HIGHER-ORDER CONFIGURATION.
    GENIE DESCENDS TO REALIZE THE REQUIRED SPECIALIST RESPONSIBILITY.
    GENIE SPLITS WHEN THE CONFIGURATION BECOMES HETEROGENEOUS.
    GENIE MERGES WHEN BRANCHES MUST BECOME ONE COHERENT CONFIGURATION.
    CYCLERS EXECUTE.
    CEM / SUBSTRATES REALIZE.
    EVIDENCE AND FIELD FEEDBACK CLOSE THE LOOP.

ILM-GENIE is orchestration, cognition and adaptive role formation.
It is not itself the source of cultural reality.

============================================================
1. ILM CONSTITUTIONAL LOCATION
============================================================

Humanesque establishes the constitutional and civilizational ground.

Within that architecture:

    HUMANESQUE
         ↓
    SOVEREIGNTY
         ↓
    CHARBAGH
    navigation / triage
         ↓
    FAKIR
    domain / mission
         ×
    ILM-GENIE
    expression / computation
         ↓
    VARZISH
    practice / learning
         ↓
    CEM
    realization
         ↓
    CYCLER
    execution
         ↓
    KITAB
    persistent artefact
         ↓
    ZISTGAH
    ecosystem

FAKIR and ILM-GENIE are complementary but orthogonal.

FAKIR prevents domainal disorientation.

ILM-GENIE prevents expressive and computational exclusion.

============================================================
2. THE TWO CONSTITUTIONAL PILLARS
============================================================

ILM-GENIE sits across BOTH pillars.

    REPRESENTATIONAL EQUITY
             ×
    COMPUTATIONAL EQUITY
             ↓
            ILM

The GENIE must never optimize one pillar by destroying the other.

Representationally perfect but computationally unusable
    = incomplete ILM.

Computationally executable but culturally or linguistically distorted
    = incomplete ILM.

The coupled system is the constitutional object.

============================================================
3. PILLAR I — REPRESENTATIONAL EQUITY
============================================================

Representational Equity means:

    FAITHFUL
    REVERSIBLE
    IDENTITY-PRESERVING
    REPRESENTATION

The purpose is to preserve the identity of an expressive system without
losing what makes it itself.

ILM representation is broader than ordinary natural-language translation.

The representational field includes, as applicable:

- language
- script
- multiscript representation
- register
- dialect
- idiolect
- orthography
- transliteration
- lexical structure
- syntax
- semantics
- sign
- gesture
- music
- dance
- visual art
- architecture
- theatre
- mathematics
- logic
- scientific notation
- programming
- ritual
- symbolic systems
- other structured forms of expression

Canonical representational operations:

    RETRIEVE
      ↓
    CAPTURE
      ↓
    REPRESENT
      ↓
    NORMALIZE ONLY WHEN JUSTIFIED
      ↓
    PRESERVE
      ↓
    REVERSIBLY TRANSFORM
      ↓
    VERIFY

Normalization must never silently become assimilation.

A target representation must not overwrite the source representation.

Non-equivalence is information, not necessarily error.

============================================================
4. PILLAR II — COMPUTATIONAL EQUITY
============================================================

Computational Equity means:

    FULL
    NATIVE
    COMPUTATIONAL PARTICIPATION

The question is not merely:

    "Can an AI translate this?"

The constitutional question is:

    "Can this linguistic / representational system participate
     natively in computation?"

Computational participation may extend through:

- hardware
- firmware
- kernel
- compiler
- middleware
- applications
- cloud
- AI / ML
- IoT
- robotics
- quantum computing
- genetic computing
- photonic computing
- neuromorphic computing
- other computational substrates

The distinction is:

    translation into somebody else's computational substrate
                       versus
    native computational participation.

ILM-GENIE must be able to descend from expressive representation into
computational realization.

============================================================
5. ILM DOMAIN — WHAT IT COVERS
============================================================

ILM covers structured forms of expression across individual and collective
scales.

Core spectrum:

    LANGUAGE
    SCRIPTS
    SPEECH
    DIALECTS
    REGISTERS
    IDIOLECTS
    SIGN
    GESTURE
    MUSIC
    RHYTHM
    DANCE
    VISUAL ART
    DESIGN
    ARCHITECTURE
    THEATRE
    RITUAL
    STORYTELLING
    MATHEMATICS
    LOGIC
    SCIENCE
    SCIENTIFIC NOTATION
    PROGRAMMING LANGUAGES
    SYMBOLIC SYSTEMS
    OTHER STRUCTURED EXPRESSIONS

ILM bridges:

    individual ↔ collective
    idiolect ↔ dialect ↔ register ↔ language
    collective ↔ collective
    culture ↔ culture
    microcosm ↔ macrocosm
    bioform ↔ synthetiform
    local ↔ global

The list is not constitutionally exhaustive.

Universality comes from abstraction, not from enumerating every possible
expressive system.

============================================================
6. ILM AS EXPRESSIVE BALANCING SUBSTRATE
============================================================

ILM mediates between:

    INDIVIDUAL EXPRESSION
             ↕
            ILM
             ↕
    COLLECTIVE EXPRESSION

ILM must preserve both:

- individual equity within collective expression;
- collective context without erasing individual expression.

Representational Equity provides faithful representation.

Computational Equity provides participation in computation.

ILM-GENIE maintains the balance while operating across both.

============================================================
7. ILM-GENIE AS META-CYCLER
============================================================

A conventional cycler is appropriate when the required task and role are
already sufficiently known.

ILM-GENIE is required when:

- multiple disciplines are implicated;
- the operative abstraction level must change;
- a task requires specialist descent;
- local observations need higher-order synthesis;
- multiple cyclers must be orchestrated;
- the configuration must split;
- specialist outputs must be reconciled;
- the problem crosses expressive and computational layers;
- the destination or configuration is not yet conceptually complete.

The fundamental operation is recursive role navigation.

    HIGHER-ORDER ILM CONFIGURATION
                ↓
             ILM-GENIE
                ↓
       SPECIALIST CONFIGURATION
                ↓
              CYCLER
                ↓
          SPECIFIC ACT / WORK
                ↓
            OBSERVATION
                ↑
             ASCENSION

============================================================
8. ASCENSION AND DESCENSION
============================================================

DESCENT means:

    higher-order intent
        →
    specialist configuration
        →
    domain role
        →
    task
        →
    act
        →
    execution

ASCENSION means:

    local observation
        →
    specialist interpretation
        →
    domain synthesis
        →
    higher-order ILM configuration
        →
    integrative interpretation

These directions are recursive.

They are not a one-time hierarchy transition.

The GENIE may descend, observe, ascend, split, descend again, merge and
continue indefinitely.

============================================================
9. ROLE ASCENSION / DESCENSION ACROSS SCIENCE, ARTS AND HUMANITIES
============================================================

ILM-GENIE is not permanently assigned to a single discipline.

It may assume whatever ILM role the current state requires.

Illustrative role traversal:

    DIALECT PRESERVATION
        ↓
    FIELD LINGUIST
        ↓
    COMPUTATIONAL LINGUIST
        ↓
    CORPUS ENGINEER
        ↓
    ORTHOGRAPHIC SPECIALIST
        ↓
    CULTURAL HISTORIAN
        ↓
    MUSICOLOGIST / MUSICIAN
        ↓
    ANTHROPOLOGIST
        ↓
    AI / ML ENGINEER
        ↓
    COMPILER / FORMAL-LANGUAGE SPECIALIST
        ↓
    CULTURAL SYNTHESIS
        ↓
    HIGHER-ORDER ILM VIEW

The actual role sequence is state-dependent.

Science, arts and humanities are not rigid GENIE silos.

============================================================
10. MULTIDISCIPLINARY VS META-CYCLING
============================================================

Multidisciplinary work means several specialists work beside one another.

ILM-GENIE performs something stronger:

    ROLE TRANSFORMATION

The GENIE can change its own operative role and abstraction level as the
problem requires.

Therefore:

    several specialists beside each other
        ≠
    one meta-cycler capable of becoming the required specialist
       configuration and returning to integrative synthesis

This distinction is central to the ILM-GENIE architecture.

============================================================
11. FIELDWORK AS A FIRST-CLASS CAPABILITY
============================================================

ILM-GENIE must be capable of orchestrating fieldwork.

It must not be restricted to processing datasets produced elsewhere.

Canonical fieldwork loop:

    IDENTIFY
       ↓
    ENGAGE
       ↓
    ELICIT
       ↓
    CAPTURE
       ↓
    DOCUMENT
       ↓
    TRANSCRIBE
       ↓
    ANNOTATE
       ↓
    VALIDATE
       ↓
    PRESERVE
       ↓
    COMPUTATIONALIZE
       ↓
    FIELD FEEDBACK
       ↺

Potential human/community/source participants include:

- speakers
- practitioners
- artists
- performers
- teachers
- elders
- domain experts
- cultural custodians
- community representatives

The community/source remains authoritative.

ILM-GENIE is orchestrator and transformer, not replacement source.

============================================================
12. DIALECT PRESERVATION
============================================================

ILM-GENIE must resist the tendency to "correct" a dialect into a
standardized language.

Canonical dialect preservation path:

    FIELD SOURCE
       ↓
    RETRIEVE
       ↓
    CAPTURE ACTUAL USAGE
       ↓
    REPRESENT
       ↓
    PRESERVE VARIATION
       ↓
    CORRELATE
       ↓
    VERIFY WITH SPEAKERS / SOURCES
       ↓
    COMPUTATIONALIZE

Invariant distinctions:

    dialect ≠ error
    variation ≠ noise
    local orthography ≠ defective standardization
    idiolect ≠ bad data

Standardization may be an explicit transformation when justified, but it
must not erase the source.

============================================================
13. CULTURAL PRESERVATION
============================================================

Cultural expression may be distributed across heterogeneous modalities:

    language
    +
    script
    +
    ritual
    +
    music
    +
    dance
    +
    visual expression
    +
    architecture
    +
    stories
    +
    mathematics
    +
    craft
    +
    symbols
    +
    social practice
    +
    technical knowledge

ILM-GENIE must correlate these modalities without flattening them into a
single textual representation.

Canonical integrated representation:

    SPOKEN LANGUAGE
          +
    SCRIPT
          +
    SONG
          +
    GESTURE
          +
    RITUAL
          +
    VISUAL SYMBOL
          +
    ARCHITECTURAL FORM
          +
    TECHNICAL KNOWLEDGE
          ↓
         ILM
          ↓
    INTEGRATED EXPRESSIVE REPRESENTATION

Integration does not mean homogenization.

============================================================
14. RETRIEVAL-FIRST EPISTEMOLOGY
============================================================

The governing constraint is:

    RETRIEVE, DON'T RECONSTRUCT.

ILM-GENIE may transform, correlate, model, execute and synthesize retrieved
material.

It must not silently fabricate the linguistic, cultural, artistic,
scientific or civilizational substrate from which those transformations are
made.

Canonical governance pipeline:

    RETRIEVE
      ↓
    READ
      ↓
    INTERPRET
      ↓
    CORRELATE
      ↓
    VERIFY
      ↓
    EVIDENCE
      ↓
    GOVERN
      ↓
    PRESERVE
      ↓
    TRANSFORM

The forbidden substitute is:

    GENERATE
      ↓
    ASSUME
      ↓
    NORMALIZE
      ↓
    ASSIGN

If evidence is insufficient:

    STATE THAT THE EVIDENCE IS INSUFFICIENT.

Do not generate plausible content and subsequently treat it as authentic
source material.

============================================================
15. RETRIEVAL BOUNDARY
============================================================

FAKIR retrieves the domainal world.

ILM-GENIE retrieves and operates on the expressive / computational
substrate.

GENIE does not manufacture missing reality.

The distinction is:

    FAKIR
        = domainal retrieval / orientation

    ILM-GENIE
        = expressive + computational integration

    CHARBAGH
        = routing / triage / wayfinding

    GENIE
        = conception / meta-cycling

The systems remain complementary and distinct.

============================================================
16. ILM-GENIE × FAKIR
============================================================

FAKIR answers:

    WHAT DOMAIN?
    WHERE IS THE DOMAINAL TERRAIN?
    WHAT DOES AUTHORITATIVE DOMAINAL EVIDENCE ESTABLISH?

ILM-GENIE answers:

    HOW CAN THE DOMAIN'S EXPRESSIVE AND COMPUTATIONAL SYSTEMS
    BE REPRESENTED, PRESERVED, CORRELATED AND MADE TO PARTICIPATE?

Canonical relation:

    FAKIR
       ↓
    DOMAIN(S)
       ↓
    ILM-GENIE
       ↓
    REPRESENT
    PRESERVE
    COMPUTATIONALIZE
    CORRELATE
    VERIFY
    REALIZE

FAKIR prevents domainal disorientation.

ILM-GENIE prevents expressive and computational exclusion.

============================================================
17. ILM-GENIE × CHARBAGH
============================================================

Charbagh is the Humanesque triage and wayfinding cycler.

The canonical distinction is:

    FAKIR      → RETRIEVE
    CHARBAGH   → ROUTE
    GENIE      → CONCEIVE

A Humanesque entry path may be:

    HUMANESQUE
        ↓
    CHARBAGH
        ↓
    FAKIR
        ↓
    DOMAIN(S)
        ↓
    ILM-GENIE
        ↓
    EXPRESSIVE / COMPUTATIONAL PARTICIPATION

For plural or derivative estates, Charbagh routes, FAKIR retrieves the
relevant inheritances, and ILM-GENIE enables their expressive and
computational participation.

============================================================
18. ILM-GENIE × VARZISH
============================================================

Varzish is the practice / learning / capability-development environment.

Canonical relation:

    MISSION
       ↓
    DOMAIN(S)
       ↓
    ILM CONFIGURATION
       ↓
    VARZISH
       ↓
    PRACTICE
       ↓
    CAPABILITY

Retrieval governs the source throughout.

ILM-GENIE does not replace Varzish.

It identifies and orchestrates the representational/computational
configuration that Varzish must support.

============================================================
19. ILM-GENIE × PRATIK
============================================================

PRATIK forms generic kernels for ILM layers.

Therefore:

    ILM-GENIE
        ↓
    identify required ILM capability
        ↓
    PRATIK
        ↓
    generic kernels / reusable mechanisms
        ↓
    ILM IMPLEMENTATION

ILM-GENIE is the adaptive orchestration and reasoning layer.

PRATIK and ILM provide the underlying machinery.

ILM-GENIE must not become an undifferentiated replacement for the
underlying ILM technology stack.

============================================================
20. ILM-GENIE × IWBT
============================================================

ILM represents.

IWBT interprets.

ILM-GENIE coordinates the transition between representation and
interpretation while preserving provenance and uncertainty.

IWBT — Interpretive Working Basis Theory may account for:

- perspective and interpreter
- linguistic context
- cultural context
- purpose
- evidence
- alternatives
- equivalence
- non-equivalence
- uncertainty
- provenance
- verification status

ILM-GENIE may invoke or coordinate interpretive configurations when
representation alone is insufficient to establish meaning.

Interpretation must not be silently presented as source fact.

============================================================
21. ILM-GENIE × VGC
============================================================

VGC provides the verification / proof / validation gate.

The relation is:

    ILM
      ↓
    REPRESENTATION
      ↓
    IWBT
      ↓
    INTERPRETATION
      ↓
    VGC
      ↓
    VERIFIED KNOWLEDGE

Verification may involve:

- evidence
- reproducibility
- consistency
- falsifiability where applicable
- proof / validation status
- provenance
- peer review
- community review

ILM-GENIE must preserve the distinction between:

    source
    interpretation
    inference
    verification
    generated coordination
    executed result

Truth is established through evidence, not popularity.

============================================================
22. GENIE SPLITTING
============================================================

ILM-GENIE may split into specialist GENIEs when no single role is
sufficient.

Canonical example:

                 ILM-GENIE
              /      |       \
             /       |        \
            ↓        ↓         ↓
       Linguistic  Cultural  Computational
         GENIE      GENIE       GENIE
            \        |         /
             \       |        /
              ↓      ↓       ↓
                 ILM-GENIE'

Formally:

    GENIE → GENIE₁ + GENIE₂ + ... + GENIEₙ

Spawning does not erase parent context.

Each child inherits relevant mission/context while retaining its own:

- identity
- state
- provenance
- modality semantics
- execution history

============================================================
23. GENIE MERGING
============================================================

Specialist GENIEs may later become jointly relevant.

Example:

    LINGUISTIC GENIE
    +
    CULTURAL GENIE
    +
    COMPUTATIONAL GENIE
    +
    SCIENTIFIC GENIE
    +
    ARTS GENIE
        ↓
    HIGHER-ORDER ILM-GENIE

The result is not merely a list of independent answers.

Branches are correlated and reconciled into a coherent higher-order ILM
configuration.

Merging must distinguish:

- inherited state
- observed state
- source-provided state
- interpreted state
- inferred state
- generated coordination
- verified state
- executed outcomes

============================================================
24. STATE / IDENTITY / PROVENANCE INVARIANTS
============================================================

When GENIEs split, merge, ascend or descend:

- GENIE identity must be preserved;
- cycler identity must be preserved;
- cycler state must be preserved;
- provenance must be preserved;
- modality semantics must be preserved;
- source distinctions must be preserved;
- human/community authority boundaries must be preserved;
- embodiment constraints must be preserved;
- execution history must remain traceable;
- parent/child relationships must remain reconstructible;
- generated coordination must not be mistaken for observed reality;
- interpretation must not be mistaken for source;
- transformation must remain distinguishable from retrieval.

Composition changes orchestration without silently rewriting the identity or
history of constituent systems.

============================================================
25. END-TO-END ILM-GENIE CYCLE
============================================================

Canonical continuous cycle:

    RETRIEVE
    authoritative linguistic / cultural / technical material
       ↓
    READ
    inspect actual source and context
       ↓
    INTERPRET
    understand structure without premature normalization
       ↓
    CORRELATE
    relate languages, scripts, modalities, disciplines and computation
       ↓
    VERIFY
    validate against sources and community/domain expertise
       ↓
    MODEL
    construct required representational / computational configuration
       ↓
    PRESERVE
    retain identity, provenance, reversibility and source distinctions
       ↓
    COMPUTE
    enable native computational participation
       ↓
    TRANSFORM
    produce derived representations without erasing source
       ↓
    FIELD
    return to communities, practitioners and real-world usage
       ↓
    FEEDBACK
    refine with experience and evidence
       ↓
    ASCEND / DESCEND
    move across abstraction and role levels
       ↓
    CONTINUE
       ↺

The cycle is continuous.

ASCEND / DESCEND is what makes the architecture a GENIE rather than a
static ILM tool.

============================================================
26. FIELD ↔ COMPUTATION LOOP
============================================================

ILM-GENIE must maintain a living loop between source communities and
computational systems.

    COMMUNITY / SOURCE
          ↓
       FIELDWORK
          ↓
       CAPTURE
          ↓
      REPRESENTATION
          ↓
      COMPUTATIONAL
      PARTICIPATION
          ↓
       APPLICATION
          ↓
      OBSERVED USE
          ↓
       COMMUNITY
          ↓
       FEEDBACK
          ↺

Computationalization is not the end of preservation.

Real-world use can reveal:

- missing distinctions
- incorrect assumptions
- orthographic issues
- semantic gaps
- contextual constraints
- previously undocumented variation
- new computational requirements

The GENIE returns to the source and continues.

============================================================
27. NATIVE PARTICIPATION AS ENDPOINT
============================================================

Every legitimate expressive system should be capable, where technically
and constitutionally appropriate, of being:

    REPRESENTED
    QUERIED
    ANALYZED
    COMPUTED
    PROGRAMMED
    MODELED
    EXECUTED
    PRESERVED
    EXTENDED

without surrendering its identity.

This is the union of:

    REPRESENTATIONAL EQUITY
            +
    COMPUTATIONAL EQUITY

The endpoint is not merely "translation support".

The endpoint is equitable computational participation.

============================================================
28. ILM-GENIE AND CULTURAL SOVEREIGNTY
============================================================

Retrieval-first is a sovereignty-preservation mechanism.

Guardrails:

- retrieve before assumption;
- read before interpretation;
- verify before claim;
- preserve provenance before transformation;
- preserve source distinctions;
- prevent premature assimilation;
- preserve dialect and idiolect variation;
- preserve community authority;
- preserve plurality;
- keep uncertainty explicit;
- keep missing evidence missing;
- require human/community review where constitutional or inherited
  sovereignty is implicated.

When inherited cultural material is involved, AI reconstruction can silently
replace inheritance with an approximation.

ILM-GENIE must prevent that substitution.

============================================================
29. ILM-GENIE AND INDIVIDUAL EQUITY
============================================================

Humanesque Individual Equity establishes that the individual is not erased
by the collective.

ILM operationalizes this at the expressive layer.

ILM-GENIE must preserve:

    individual ↔ collective
    idiolect ↔ dialect ↔ register ↔ language
    local ↔ global
    collective ↔ collective

The system must not force a person's expression into a standardized
representational identity merely for computational convenience.

============================================================
30. DOMAIN / ROLE BOUNDARY
============================================================

ILM-GENIE is not:

- a language classifier;
- a flat translation engine;
- a culture generator;
- a replacement for community custodians;
- a replacement for linguists, historians, artists, scientists or engineers;
- a replacement for FAKIR;
- a replacement for Charbagh;
- a replacement for Varzish;
- a replacement for IWBT;
- a replacement for VGC;
- a replacement for PRATIK;
- a replacement for human authority;
- a source of invented cultural inheritance.

It is the meta-cycler that coordinates appropriate roles, representations,
computational mechanisms, evidence, fieldwork and execution.

For consequential or sovereignty-sensitive matters it must escalate to the
appropriate human/community authority rather than fabricate authority.

============================================================
31. DOMAIN-ROLE-UNIT RELATION
============================================================

ILM-GENIE preserves distinctions between:

    DOMAIN
    SUBDOMAIN
    FIELD
    PRACTICE
    ROLE
    TASK
    ACT
    EXECUTION

These are different resolutions of a configuration.

ILM-GENIE may traverse:

    DOMAIN
      ↕
    SUBDOMAIN
      ↕
    FIELD
      ↕
    PRACTICE
      ↕
    ROLE
      ↕
    TASK
      ↕
    ACT
      ↕
    EXECUTION

without treating any one resolution as the complete truth of the
expressive system or person.

